PROPOSED DIFF · r0/r6-idiom-history/law-probe.mjs · row R1 · reported MOVED

The record is frozen: this is a PROPOSAL banked beside the lane's research, never an edit to
`loop/r0/`. The r0 row R1 is reported MOVED, not re-cut in place, and not re-worded to pass.

WHY. R1 asserts "every chromatic token that paints in BOTH themes carries a dark arm", born
RED against `--color-focus-sketch`. MRK-LIVE refutes the law rather than satisfying it, and
the refutation is arithmetic on painted bytes over four grounds x two themes
(`../logs/B-grounds-*.json`, `../logs/C-boardring-*.json`, `../probe/token-table.mjs`):

  one value #3a7bc4        chrome 4.19 / 4.29 light, 4.38 / 4.29 dark
                           board  3.67 / 3.34 light, 3.72 / 3.48 dark
                           SPREAD over all eight readings: 1.04
  a dark arm (#6aabeb)     SPREAD 4.52 — the mark weighs four times more at night
  every candidate clears WCAG 1.4.11's 3:1 on every ground in both themes

So the law's premise ("a token painting in both themes NEEDS a dark arm") does not hold as an
accessibility law on this tree. What the row actually caught was a COMMENT that claimed a dark
arm the token has never had. Re-base the row onto the defect it found.

THE PROPOSED ROW. Strictly stronger than the incumbent: it catches the original defect AND
every future one of the same class, in both directions.

--- a/law-probe.mjs
+++ b/law-probe.mjs
@@
 law(
   "R1",
-  "every chromatic token that paints in BOTH themes carries a dark arm",
-  "index.css --color-focus-sketch:219 — its own comment claims 'Dark mode keeps crayon-blue'",
+  "every chromatic token's comment tells the truth about its themes",
+  "index.css --color-focus-sketch:219 — declared once in :root, comment claims 'Dark mode keeps crayon-blue'",
   "RED",
   () => {
     const css = read("src/assets/index.css");
     const darkAt = css.indexOf("\n.dark");
-    const inDark = css.slice(darkAt).includes("--color-focus-sketch:");
-    return {
-      ok: inDark,
-      detail: inDark
-        ? "declared in .dark"
-        : "declared ONLY in :root — the focus ring paints #3a7bc4 at night, and the comment says otherwise",
-    };
+    const inDark = css.slice(darkAt).includes("--color-focus-sketch:");
+    // The comment that sits above the :root declaration, whatever it now says.
+    const decl = css.indexOf("--color-focus-sketch:");
+    const comment = css.slice(decl, css.indexOf("\n", css.indexOf("*/", decl)) + 1);
+    // A token declared ONLY in :root must not claim an arm; a token WITH an arm must name
+    // its arm's measured reading. Both directions, so neither a lying comment nor a silent
+    // arm can pass.
+    const claimsArm = /dark mode|at night|\.dark/i.test(comment);
+    const namesReading = /\d+\.\d+\s*(:1|ratio)/i.test(comment);
+    const ok = inDark ? claimsArm && namesReading : !claimsArm && namesReading;
+    return {
+      ok,
+      detail: inDark
+        ? `declared in .dark; comment ${claimsArm ? "names the arm" : "is SILENT about it"}, ` +
+          `${namesReading ? "with a measured reading" : "with NO measured reading"}`
+        : `declared ONLY in :root; comment ${claimsArm ? "CLAIMS an arm it does not have" : "correctly claims none"}, ` +
+          `${namesReading ? "with a measured reading" : "with NO measured reading"}`,
+    };
   },
 );

